On Wayland a window asks the compositor for a new state (full screen, maximized, normal) only
once the compositor has answered its last request and Chromium has acked that answer; one asked
meanwhile changes the window's own state at once, as before, and waits, the latest one only.
sway 1.9 configures a window that leaves full screen before acking its entry at the size it
entered at, and one that enters before acking its exit at the size it left at, as its
should_configure compares with the state the unacked configure never applied; it then keeps the
size its floating window commits, so a page's full screen left quickly brought the window back
at the output's size, swinging between the two first (#1714). A roundtrip after each request
lets the configures it brings, and sway's answer to the commit that acks them, arrive first.
